## 🛠️ Project Overview

**XeroxFlow** is a multi-tenant print-queue web application built for local print/xerox shops. It allows shop owners to register their shop, set up pricing, and display a dynamic QR code. Customers scan the QR code to access a print dropbox page, upload a PDF document, preview/calculate costs in real-time, and optionally pay via UPI. The uploaded print job then appears in the shop owner's live queue dashboard for immediate printing.

### Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 16.2.1 (React 19.2.4)
- **Database / Backend:** Supabase (utilizes auth, storage, and real-time database updates)
- **Styling:** CSS via TailwindCSS v4 with `@tailwindcss/postcss`
- **Component & Icons:** Lucide React
- **Specific Utility Packages:**
  - `pdf-lib` (client-side page count / metadata calculation)
  - `react-pdf` (render PDF previews if needed)
  - `react-qr-code` (display dynamic shop QR code)
  - `sonner` (toast notifications)

