## 📁 Codebase Architecture

Here is the breakdown of files in the project and their core purposes:

1. **`lib/supabaseClient.ts`**
   - Configures and exports the Supabase client using environment variables.

2. **`app/layout.tsx`** & **`app/globals.css`**
   - Main root layout and global styles configuration.

3. **`app/page.tsx`**
   - Public landing page. Auto-redirects to `/dashboard` if a session is present.

4. **`app/login/page.tsx`** & **`app/signup/page.tsx`**
   - User authentication pages for shop owners to log in or register a new store.

5. **`app/dashboard/page.tsx`**
   - The shop owner dashboard containing:
     - Profile/Banner Card (tapable, with dynamic auto-scaling shop name via container queries, location, logo, and rating display).
     - Settings editing popup (for Shop Name, Location, and custom Logo uploads).
     - Manage Add-ons settings modal (add and configure custom lamination, binding, etc. items and their price tags).
     - Real-time print queue (listening to PostgreSQL `orders` table updates).
     - Shop settings editor (pricing matrix for single/double-sided black & white or color prints, and store UPI ID).
     - Printable QR code containing the shop's customer portal link, alongside a clickable direct testing hyperlink.
     - PDF document printer utility (renders file within a hidden iframe for print spooling).
     - Shows warning alerts for expired or ending subscriptions in the Live Queue section.
     - Displays subscription status card inside Profile Settings modal.
     - Hides all printable customer documents when subscription expires, rendering a lock notice instead.
     - Renders a red "Updates paused" indicator when subscription expires.

6. **`app/shop/[shopId]/page.tsx`**
   - The public dropbox page for a specific shop.
   - Performs anonymous authentication if not already logged in to allow file uploads.
   - Displays a dynamic checkable add-ons list once a PDF is selected.
   - Restructured layout placing the file upload box at the top, followed by settings (copies, color) and customer details (name, optional phone).
   - Dynamic top branding that displays the shop logo and uppercase shop name.
   - Uploads PDFs to `xerox-files` storage bucket and saves details to the `orders` database. Appends selected add-on names to the `customer_name` string.
   - Displays a success state with a UPI link (`upi://pay`) for easy QR/deeplink payments.
   - Integrates a simple star-rating and feedback submission modal on successful upload.
   - Logs customer upload file sizes to LocalStorage under `xeroxflow_storage_logs`.
   - Blocks uploads with a "Service Suspended" overlay if shop subscription is expired.

7. **`app/admin/page.tsx`**
   - The admin management console dashboard.
   - Logs in using static administrator credentials (`admin@xeroxflow.com` / `admin123`).
   - Lists active print shops registered.
   - Displays current storage utilization (audited from folder files listing) and last 24h upload volume (audited from local storage upload logs).
   - Features a shop provisioning form to register new print shop owner credentials and assign subscription terms.
   - Features an inline subscription plan details editor linked to the `plans` table.
   - Features sorting, searching, interactive tag modals, and plan creators.
   - Allows negative custom month inputs for expired test configurations.

8. **`app/renew/page.tsx`**
   - The renewal information page.
   - Lists subscription plans dynamically fetched from the `plans` table.
   - Displays contact details of the system administrator (Omkar Varpe).

